10662446,2024-11-02,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Unable to get your credit report or credit score,Other problem getting your report or credit score,"I am writing to formally lodge a complaint regarding Equifaxs refusal to grant me access to my personal credit report, as required by federal law, despite my provision of a valid government-issued photo ID and Social Security card for identity verification purposes. This denial not only hinders my consumer rights but also potentially violates several key federal laws. 

1. Violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), 15 U.S.C. 1681 et seq., Under the FCRA, consumers are legally entitled to obtain a free annual credit report from each of the three credit reporting agencies ( CRAs ), including Equifax. This right is outlined in Section 612 ( a ) of the FCRA, which mandates that every CRA provide a free copy of the consumers file upon request, subject only to identity verification requirements. Despite my submission of legitimate identification documents, Equifax has failed to provide my credit report, effectively obstructing my lawful right to review my financial information. 

2. Breach of the Consumer Financial Protection Act of 2010 ( CFPA ), 12 U.S.C. 5481 et seq., The CFPA prohibits unfair, deceptive, or abusive acts or practices ( UDAAPs ) by financial institutions and credit reporting agencies. Equifaxs refusal to honor my request and failure to provide a valid reason for the denial constitutes an unfair practice, especially since I have met all reasonable identification verification requirements. This denial limits my ability to manage, monitor, and safeguard my financial health and data security. 

3. Unfair Practices under the Federal Trade Commission Act ( FTCA ), 15 U.S.C. 45 ( a ), The FTCA also prohibits unfair or deceptive acts or practices affecting commerce. By blocking access to my credit report despite adequate identification, Equifax has engaged in actions that unreasonably deny me access to information that could impact my financial decision-making.

Immediate Action Requested, I respectfully request that Equifax immediately comply with federal laws and fulfill my request to access my credit file. I also request that the CFPB investigate this matter to prevent further infringements on consumer rights. If Equifax continues to obstruct my access to my credit file, I am prepared to escalate this matter, including filing complaints with the Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ) and potentially seeking further legal recourse to safeguard my consumer rights.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10027,,Web,2024-11-02,Closed with explanation,Yes
