10761714,2024-11-11,Debt collection,Auto debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was result of identity theft,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ), I am filing a formal complaint against **Jefferson Capital Systems , LLC** for multiple violations, including unauthorized reporting of my personal financial information, **lack of permissible purpose** for accessing and reporting my information, **identity theft**, **defamation**, and **damages to my credit worthiness, reputation, and privacy**. The actions of **Jefferson Capital** have not only undermined my confidence in the banking system but have caused significant emotional and financial distress.

Below, I outline the violations and the compensation I am seeking for each.

-- - # # # **1. Lack of Permissible Purpose for Accessing and Reporting My Personal Information** Under the **Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) **, third parties are only permitted to access and report my personal financial information if they have a **legitimate permissible purpose**. **Jefferson Capital** has reported information about my debt to the credit bureaus, but I have **never authorized** them to access or report this information.

I request the following from **Jefferson Capital** : - **Proof of a permissible purpose** for accessing and reporting my personal information to the credit bureaus, - **Proof of a wet signature** on any document related to the transfer or collection of this debt.

