10797890,2024-11-14,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Was not notified of investigation status or results,"XX/XX/XXXX Subject : Formal Dispute of Inaccurate Late Payments on XXXX Mortgage Account Dear CFPB, I am writing to formally dispute the inaccurate reporting of late payments on my XXXX mortgage account, reported by TransUnion. I previously filed a dispute regarding these discrepancies, yet no corrections have been made to reflect the accurate payment history. This letter serves as a second dispute request, and I am asking for a full investigation in compliance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), as per 15 USC 1681i ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), which mandates that credit reporting agencies must conduct a thorough investigation upon receiving a consumer dispute.

Summary of Discrepancies Upon reviewing my payment records, I found no late payments on this account, yet each bureau reports different late payment dates : TransUnion and XXXX report late payments in XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX, as well as XXXX, XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXX. 
XXXX shows XXXX late payments in XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXX. 
These discrepancies violate the FCRAs accuracy requirement and negatively impact my credit score. Therefore, I request a full investigation of these entries and a correction to accurately reflect a Paid As Agreed Never Late status.

Request for Documentation and Investigation Process Pursuant to 15 USC 1681i ( a ) ( 6 ) ( B ) ( iii ), I request a detailed description of the investigation process your agency conducted for this dispute, as required by the FCRA. Additionally, under 15 USC 1681 ( a ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ), I request that all transactional information regarding this account be reviewed for accuracy.

